.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Universal CI/CD gatekeeper and AI coding agent diff sentinel
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "discipline check"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
Run the configured gates. Exit 0 = pass, 1 = violations, 2 = could not check
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.PP
\fBdiscipline check\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-override\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-suite\fR] [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-commit\fR] [\fB\-\-commit\-range\fR] [\fB\-\-staged\fR] [\fB\-\-pr\-body\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-pr\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-warnings\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-overrides\fR] [\fB\-\-advisory\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-actor\fR] [\fB\-\-directive\-sources\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-json\-out\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-report\-gitlab\fR] [\fB\-\-report\-junit\fR] [\fB\-\-report\-sarif\fR] [\fB\-\-bench\-provenance\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-cross\-host\-bench\fR] [\fB\-\-bench\-base\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-bench\-head\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-baseline\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-baseline\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.PP
\fBOPTIONS\fR
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR [default: discipline.toml]
Path to discipline.toml. Absent file = built\-in defaults (`discipline gates` lists them)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_CONFIG\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-override\fR \fI<CONFIG_OVERRIDE>\fR
Inline TOML merged over the file (tables merge, lists append, scalars replace)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_CONFIG_OVERRIDE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\fR \fI<ENABLE>\fR
Gate ids to force on (comma separated)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_ENABLE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\fR \fI<DISABLE>\fR
Gate ids to force off (comma separated)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_DISABLE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-suite\fR \fI<SUITE>\fR [default: all]
Which check suite to run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
all
.IP \(bu 2
agent\-guard
.IP \(bu 2
hygiene
.IP \(bu 2
integrity
.IP \(bu 2
quality
.IP \(bu 2
verification
.IP \(bu 2
bench
.RE
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-base\fR \fI<BASE>\fR
Base branch or commit to measure the change against (auto\-detected in CI if omitted)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_BASE_REF\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fI<COMMIT>\fR
Specific commit to inspect (compares against parent commit <sha>~1)
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\-range\fR \fI<COMMIT_RANGE>\fR
Commit range to inspect (<before>..<after> or <before>...<after>)
.TP
\fB\-\-staged\fR
Inspect the index against HEAD instead (pre\-commit hook mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-pr\-body\-file\fR \fI<PR_BODY_FILE>\fR
File holding the PR body or commit message (override directives, hygiene scanning). Falls back to the PR_BODY environment variable
.TP
\fB\-\-pr\-title\fR \fI<PR_TITLE>\fR
PR title for PR\-level hygiene checks (e.g. issue\-link). Falls back to the PR_TITLE environment variable
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPR_TITLE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-warnings\fR
Treat warnings as failures
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_FAIL_ON_WARNINGS\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-overrides\fR
Treat applied overrides as failures (requires human sign\-off)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_FAIL_ON_OVERRIDES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-advisory\fR
Advisory mode: run all checks and emit reports, but exit code 0 even if violations occur
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_ADVISORY\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\-from\fR \fI<POLICY_FROM>\fR [default: head]
Which side\*(Aqs discipline.toml judges the change. `base` reads it from the base ref, so a policy edit takes effect once merged; `config\-integrity` still reports it
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
head: The configuration in the working tree (the change\*(Aqs own copy)
.IP \(bu 2
base: The configuration on the base ref
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_POLICY_FROM\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR \fI<ACTOR>\fR
Actor executing the check (for actor\-aware override authorization). Falls back to DISCIPLINE_ACTOR, GITHUB_ACTOR, GITEA_ACTOR, FORGEJO_ACTOR, GITLAB_USER_LOGIN
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_ACTOR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-directive\-sources\fR \fI<DIRECTIVE_SOURCES>\fR
Comma\-separated list of allowed directive sources (pr\-body, commits)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDISCIPLINE_DIRECTIVE_SOURCES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-trust\-workspace\fR
Trust the workspace and disable libgit2 repository owner validation (off by default, or set DISCIPLINE_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress output on success (only print output when violations are found)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: terminal]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
terminal
.IP \(bu 2
github\-summary
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
junit
.IP \(bu 2
sarif
.IP \(bu 2
gitlab
.IP \(bu 2
agent\-prompt
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-out\fR \fI<JSON_OUT>\fR
Also write the JSON report to this path, whatever \-\-format is
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-file\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FILE>\fR
Write the formatted report to this path
.TP
\fB\-\-report\-gitlab\fR \fI<REPORT_GITLAB>\fR
